# Living World Events quest texts
quest.regicide.title = Regicide
quest.regicide.short = Obtain a Tyrant’s Skull
quest.regicide.description = Hold a Blood Moon to its last stage and a crowned Tyrant comes for you. Its skull makes a fine trophy.
quest.crimson-herald.title = Reap the Reaper
quest.crimson-herald.short = Defeat the Crimson Herald in its final form
quest.crimson-herald.description = Some nights the Herald comes in the Tyrant’s place. When its scythe catches fire, it starts to reap in earnest.
quest.torn-from-herald.title = Torn from the Herald
quest.torn-from-herald.short = Obtain the Crimson Scythe
quest.torn-from-herald.description = The Herald never lets go of its scythe while it stands. Make it fall, and sometimes the blade stays behind.
quest.treasure-goblin.title = Catch Me If You Can
quest.treasure-goblin.short = Kill a Treasure Goblin
quest.treasure-goblin.description = A trail of loose coins warns you that he is already running.
quest.stolen-sack.title = The Thief’s Bag
quest.stolen-sack.short = Obtain a Stolen Sack
quest.stolen-sack.description = Now and then a Treasure Goblin bursts and drops his whole sack. The seams are stretched tight: even the thread might be worth something.
quest.sprockets-spare.title = Sprocket’s Spare
quest.sprockets-spare.short = Obtain Sprocket’s Drill
quest.sprockets-spare.description = The Broodmother sometimes drags one of Sprocket’s drills down with her. He swears he only lent it. He will never see it again.
quest.broodmother.title = The Queen Falls
quest.broodmother.short = Defeat the Broodmother in her final form
quest.broodmother.description = Sometimes, after the last wave, the Scarak queen digs up to the drill herself. The tunnels tremble long after her last shell breaks.
quest.awakening-bloodletter-awakened.title = an awakened Bloodletter
quest.awakening-bloodletter-awakened.short = Craft an awakened Bloodletter
quest.awakening-bloodletter-awakened.description = Weapon Bench, tier 3: the Bloodletter, Herald’s Ichor, 2 Tyrant Hearts and 5 mithril bars.
quest.awakening-moonfang-staff-awakened.title = an awakened Moonfang Staff
quest.awakening-moonfang-staff-awakened.short = Craft an awakened Moonfang Staff
quest.awakening-moonfang-staff-awakened.description = Arcane Bench: the Moonfang Staff, Herald’s Ichor, 2 Tyrant Hearts and 5 mithril bars.
quest.awakening-brood-stinger-awakened.title = an awakened Brood Stinger
quest.awakening-brood-stinger-awakened.short = Craft an awakened Brood Stinger
quest.awakening-brood-stinger-awakened.description = Weapon Bench, tier 3: the Brood Stinger, a Brood Gland and 5 mithril bars.
quest.awakening-sprockets-drill-awakened.title = Sprocket’s awakened drill
quest.awakening-sprockets-drill-awakened.short = Craft Sprocket’s awakened drill
quest.awakening-sprockets-drill-awakened.description = Workbench, tier 3: Sprocket’s Drill, 5 Brood Glands, 4 storm leather and 9 mithril bars.
quest.awakening.title = Awakening
quest.awakening.short = Craft any awakened weapon
quest.awakening.description = There are weapons that remember their makers. These remember what woke them.
quest.all-saplings-home.title = Every Sapling Home
quest.all-saplings-home.short = Obtain a Potted Sapling
quest.all-saplings-home.description = When every lost sapling is home, the Elder trusts you with one of them. Give it a pot and a few days.
quest.friend-in-pot.title = A Friend in a Pot
quest.friend-in-pot.short = Obtain a Sapling Buddy Pot
quest.friend-in-pot.description = Now and then a rescued sapling refuses to leave your side. Its pot goes wherever you go.
quest.red-nights.title = Red Nights
quest.red-nights.short = Collect 20 Blood Shards
quest.red-nights.description = Travelers check /lwe status for word of the next event. When the moon turns red, its monsters sometimes leave a blood shard behind.
quest.blood-charm.title = A Charm in the Dark
quest.blood-charm.short = Craft a Blood Charm
quest.blood-charm.description = Twenty shards and two moonstones, the kind a Blood Moon Champion carries. The Arcane Bench does the rest.
quest.blood-moon-omen.title = A Red Omen
quest.blood-moon-omen.short = Craft a Blood Moon Omen
quest.blood-moon-omen.description = Old hands keep the omen wrapped in cloth. They say it can call the red moon or send it away.
quest.blades-red-moon.title = Blades of the Red Moon
quest.blades-red-moon.short = Craft a Moonfang Staff or a Bloodletter
quest.blades-red-moon.description = The Moonfang Staff asks only for moonstone, cobalt and shards. The Bloodletter wants a Tyrant’s heart besides.
quest.blades-red-moon-moonfang-staff.title = a Moonfang Staff
quest.blades-red-moon-moonfang-staff.short = Craft a Moonfang Staff
quest.blades-red-moon-moonfang-staff.description = Arcane Bench: 4 moonstones, 5 cobalt bars and 2 blood shards.
quest.blades-red-moon-bloodletter.title = a Bloodletter
quest.blades-red-moon-bloodletter.short = Craft a Bloodletter
quest.blades-red-moon-bloodletter.description = Weapon Bench, tier 2: 4 moonstones, 5 cobalt bars, 2 blood shards and a Tyrant Heart.
quest.drill-scaraks.title = To the Drill’s Aid
quest.drill-scaraks.short = Kill 8 Scaraks at Sprocket’s drill
quest.drill-scaraks.description = When Sprocket sets up his drill nearby, Scaraks pour out of their tunnels to stop it. Check /lwe status to see him coming.
quest.save-the-drill.title = A Drill Worth Saving
quest.save-the-drill.short = Obtain a Mini Drill
quest.save-the-drill.description = Sprocket hands out keepsakes when the last tunnel falls silent.
quest.tinkerers-flare.title = Call for Sprocket
quest.tinkerers-flare.short = Craft a Tinkerer’s Flare
quest.tinkerers-flare.description = Sprocket is always watching for a light high above the treetops.
quest.brood-sting.title = The Brood’s Sting
quest.brood-sting.short = Craft a Brood Stinger
quest.brood-sting.description = Scarak shell plates, deep ore and thorium make an axe that stings like the brood itself. Weapon Bench, tier 2.
quest.iron-and-moon-warlord-early-head.title = a Bloodforged Warlord Helm
quest.iron-and-moon-warlord-early-head.short = Craft a Bloodforged Warlord Helm
quest.iron-and-moon-warlord-early-head.description = Armor Bench, tier 2: an iron helm, 8 blood shards, 7 deep ore and a moonstone.
quest.iron-and-moon-warlord-early-chest.title = a Bloodforged Warlord Chestplate
quest.iron-and-moon-warlord-early-chest.short = Craft a Bloodforged Warlord Chestplate
quest.iron-and-moon-warlord-early-chest.description = Armor Bench, tier 2: an iron chestplate, 13 blood shards, 12 deep ore and a moonstone.
quest.iron-and-moon-warlord-early-hands.title = Bloodforged Warlord Gauntlets
quest.iron-and-moon-warlord-early-hands.short = Craft Bloodforged Warlord Gauntlets
quest.iron-and-moon-warlord-early-hands.description = Armor Bench, tier 2: iron gauntlets, 6 blood shards, 6 deep ore and a moonstone.
quest.iron-and-moon-warlord-early-legs.title = Bloodforged Warlord Greaves
quest.iron-and-moon-warlord-early-legs.short = Craft Bloodforged Warlord Greaves
quest.iron-and-moon-warlord-early-legs.description = Armor Bench, tier 2: iron greaves, 10 blood shards, 10 deep ore and a moonstone.
quest.iron-and-moon.title = Iron and Moon
quest.iron-and-moon.short = Craft the 4 pieces of Bloodforged Warlord armor
quest.iron-and-moon.description = Deep ore gives the plates their weight. Blood shards give them their color.
quest.road-bandits.title = Unsafe Roads
quest.road-bandits.short = Kill 8 bandits during ambushes
quest.road-bandits.description = As you travel, smoke bursts around you and bandits close in. Not every ambush is theirs: sometimes it is only the local beasts.
quest.road-captain.title = The Brute in Charge
quest.road-captain.short = Kill the Bandit Brute leading an ambush
quest.road-captain.description = The bandits wait for the brute’s shout before they risk a charge.
quest.trophy-satchel.title = Room for Charms
quest.trophy-satchel.short = Craft an Accessory Pouch
quest.trophy-satchel.description = Charms, pendants and lamps need somewhere to go. A little linen and leather at the Arcane Bench will hold them all.
quest.accessory-moonstone-pendant.title = a Moonstone Pendant
quest.accessory-moonstone-pendant.short = Craft a Moonstone Pendant
quest.accessory-moonstone-pendant.description = Arcane Bench: 20 blood shards and 4 moonstones.
quest.accessory-chitin-bracer.title = a Chitin Bracer
quest.accessory-chitin-bracer.short = Craft a Chitin Bracer
quest.accessory-chitin-bracer.description = Arcane Bench: 20 deep ore and 2 Scarak shell plates.
quest.accessory-tinkerers-lamp.title = a Tinkerer’s Lamp
quest.accessory-tinkerers-lamp.short = Craft a Tinkerer’s Lamp
quest.accessory-tinkerers-lamp.description = Arcane Bench: 20 deep ore and 2 Scarak shell plates.
quest.accessory.title = Something to Wear
quest.accessory.short = Craft a Moonstone Pendant, Chitin Bracer or Tinkerer’s Lamp
quest.accessory.description = Blood Moon nights and Sprocket’s drill sites yield the stones and shells these trinkets need. Craft one at the Arcane Bench.
quest.pathfinder-pathfinder-early-head.title = a Greenwood Pathfinder Hood
quest.pathfinder-pathfinder-early-head.short = Craft a Greenwood Pathfinder Hood
quest.pathfinder-pathfinder-early-head.description = Armor Bench, tier 2: an iron helm, 15 living sap and a razorleaf.
quest.pathfinder-pathfinder-early-chest.title = a Greenwood Pathfinder Jerkin
quest.pathfinder-pathfinder-early-chest.short = Craft a Greenwood Pathfinder Jerkin
quest.pathfinder-pathfinder-early-chest.description = Armor Bench, tier 2: an iron chestplate, 25 living sap and a razorleaf.
quest.pathfinder-pathfinder-early-hands.title = Greenwood Pathfinder Gloves
quest.pathfinder-pathfinder-early-hands.short = Craft Greenwood Pathfinder Gloves
quest.pathfinder-pathfinder-early-hands.description = Armor Bench, tier 2: iron gauntlets, 12 living sap and a razorleaf.
quest.pathfinder-pathfinder-early-legs.title = Greenwood Pathfinder Leggings
quest.pathfinder-pathfinder-early-legs.short = Craft Greenwood Pathfinder Leggings
quest.pathfinder-pathfinder-early-legs.description = Armor Bench, tier 2: iron greaves, 20 living sap and a razorleaf.
quest.pathfinder.title = A Suit of Leaves
quest.pathfinder.short = Craft the 4 pieces of Greenwood Pathfinder armor
quest.pathfinder.description = Each sapling you lead home to the Kweebec Elder leaves living sap behind. It binds wooden plates where nails would split them.
quest.razorleaf-bow.title = A Bow of Green Wood
quest.razorleaf-bow.short = Craft a Razorleaf Bow
quest.razorleaf-bow.description = The Elder parts with heartwood only once every lost sapling is home. Strung with razor leaves, it bends without complaint.
character.night-chronicler.name = Yselle
character.night-chronicler.epithet = Archivist
character.village-mechanic.name = Rivet
character.village-mechanic.epithet = Village Mechanic
character.robbed-merchant.name = Mado
character.robbed-merchant.epithet = Robbed Merchant
character.road-veteran.name = Tavin
character.road-veteran.epithet = Road Veteran
character.armorer.name = Sena
character.armorer.epithet = Armorer
character.kweebec-scout.name = Brindle
character.kweebec-scout.epithet = Kweebec Scout
quest.chronicler-skull.title = The King at Dawn
quest.chronicler-skull.short = Deliver a Tyrant’s Skull to Yselle
quest.chronicler-skull.description = In a Feran village, Yselle keeps the Blood Moon ledger. Every survivor tells the same ending: if the last lantern goes out before sunrise, a crowned Tyrant steps out of the dark. But Yselle writes nothing down without proof. Until someone brings back the Tyrant’s skull, the story stays a rumor, with no date in her ledger.
quest.chronicler-ichor.title = The Herald’s Trace
quest.chronicler-ichor.short = Deliver Herald’s Ichor to Yselle
quest.chronicler-ichor.description = Yselle keeps an empty bottle beside her lamp. Blood Moon survivors all describe the Crimson Herald the same way: a burning scythe, fields on fire, and not a drop of blood, only ichor. A story that tidy makes the Archivist wary. She wants something left from that fire before she records it.
quest.chronicler-lamp.title = A Light for the Village
quest.chronicler-lamp.short = Deliver a Tinkerer’s Lamp to Yselle
quest.chronicler-lamp.description = Yselle wants a light on the square that nobody can blow out on a Blood Moon, not even her. She is ready to spend all her savings on a tinkerer’s lamp.
quest.chronicler-page.title = The Unsigned Page
quest.chronicler-page.short = Ask Tavin what he saw on the last Blood Moon
quest.chronicler-page.description = In Yselle’s Blood Moon ledger, one account is signed by no one. The Archivist turns that page quickly, and she never lets her lamp go out before dawn.
quest.chronicler-knock.title = The One Who Knocked
quest.chronicler-knock.short = Bring Tavin’s account back to Yselle
quest.chronicler-knock.description = Yselle is waiting for an answer she dreads. Someone on the road knows what happened at her door, on the night the last lantern went out.
quest.mechanic-gland.title = Under the Drill
quest.mechanic-gland.short = Deliver a Brood Gland to Rivet
quest.mechanic-gland.description = Rivet, the Village Mechanic, taps worn drill heads at his workbench in a Feran village and listens for the thin note of a hollow. His cousin Sprocket says a queen sleeps under the drills, and Rivet has circled the same depth on three maps. Before the drill goes down there, he wants to look at one of the queen’s glands.
quest.mechanic-flare.title = A Flare for Ore
quest.mechanic-flare.short = Trade a Tinkerer’s Flare to Rivet for 8 Deep Ore
quest.mechanic-flare.description = Rivet has cleared a dry corner of his workbench, the right size for a flare. Sprocket always watches the sky for one above the treetops, and the last time a drill went quiet, Rivet had no way to call him. He pays for good tools in deep ore salvaged from worn drill heads.
quest.merchant-gold.title = Missing Savings
quest.merchant-gold.short = Deliver 3 Gold Bars to Mado
quest.merchant-gold.description = Mado runs a provisions stall in a Feran village where every shelf is numbered, even the empty ones. A goblin made off with his savings while he counted flour, and the wagoner’s bill is tucked under the flour scoop. Mado jokes about it, but without those bars no wagon will supply the village.
quest.merchant-sack.title = A Familiar Seam
quest.merchant-sack.short = Deliver a Stolen Sack to Mado
quest.merchant-sack.description = Mado, the Robbed Merchant, turns sacks seam side out whenever his stall goes quiet. The one he lost has blue thread under the flap, stitched crooked by candlelight. The coins mattered, but he wants that sack back behind the counter, where he can find the blue stitch with his thumb.
quest.veteran-captain.title = Break the Line
quest.veteran-captain.short = Kill an ambush bandit captain for Tavin
quest.veteran-captain.description = Tavin, the Road Veteran, keeps the old wagon routes scratched into a plank in a Feran village. He rode escort for Mado’s wagon until the ambushes closed the road, and he still walks on the ditch side of every path. The bandits follow the brute who calls the charge. Bring that one down, and the wagons can pass again.
quest.armorer-warlord.title = The Complete Suit
quest.armorer-warlord.short = Deliver the 4 early Warlord armor pieces to Sena
quest.armorer-warlord.description = Sena, the Armorer, mends traveling gear in a Feran village and has dragged an old armor stand into the light by her bench. She once saw deep ore worked right into a Warlord plate and keeps thinking about the shoulder that had to carry it. A full suit on the stand would show her where the weight goes.
quest.armorer-moonfang.title = The Moonfang Commission
quest.armorer-moonfang.short = Deliver a Moonfang Staff to Sena
quest.armorer-moonfang.description = Sena has unrolled a strip of soft leather on her bench. The Warlord plates taught her how a blow travels, and now she wants to know how a staff of the same make balances in a caster’s hand. Travelers stop at her bench rubbing their wrists, and she suspects the answer is in the grip.
quest.scout-sapling.title = A Place to Root
quest.scout-sapling.short = Deliver 5 Living Sap and a Potted Sapling to Brindle
quest.scout-sapling.description = Brindle, the Kweebec Scout, measures the paths around a Kweebec village in patches of shade, with tools borrowed from Rivet. On the way back from the home tree, one bare turn is marked with a flat stone. The little ones slow down there in the sun, and Brindle wants roots in that ground so they have somewhere cool to stop.
dialogue.chronicler-skull-ready.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.chronicler-skull-ready.bye = See you later.
dialogue.chronicler-skull-ready.context = On a Blood Moon, if the last lantern goes out before dawn, the Tyrant comes. Bring me its skull for the ledger, and I’ll give that story a date.
dialogue.chronicler-skull-ready.page1 = That old bone still holds the red light. May I turn it over and look for the crown’s marks?
dialogue.chronicler-skull-handoff.act = Here, take what I brought.
dialogue.chronicler-skull-handoff.bye = See you later.
dialogue.chronicler-skull-handoff.page1 = Let it rest on the ledger. I want to see where the red has settled.
dialogue.chronicler-skull-offer.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.chronicler-skull-offer.bye = See you later.
dialogue.chronicler-skull-offer.page1 = On a Blood Moon, if the last lantern goes out before dawn, the Tyrant comes. Bring me its skull for the ledger, and I’ll give that story a date.
dialogue.chronicler-skull-waiting.bye = See you later.
dialogue.chronicler-skull-waiting.page1 = The Tyrant only walks on a Blood Moon. Be outside before dawn, and stay until it falls.
dialogue.chronicler-ichor-ready.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.chronicler-ichor-ready.bye = See you later.
dialogue.chronicler-ichor-ready.previous = The marks on the skull fit the old account. I’ve left a page open for the Herald.
dialogue.chronicler-ichor-ready.context = Some nights the moon sends its Herald. They say it lit the fields with a burning scythe and left no blood behind, only ichor.
dialogue.chronicler-ichor-ready.page1 = There’s a red light in your bottle. Is that what the Herald left behind?
dialogue.chronicler-ichor-handoff.act = Here, take what I brought.
dialogue.chronicler-ichor-handoff.bye = See you later.
dialogue.chronicler-ichor-handoff.page1 = Set the bottle by the lamp. The two flames lean toward each other.
dialogue.chronicler-ichor-offer.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.chronicler-ichor-offer.bye = See you later.
dialogue.chronicler-ichor-offer.previous = The marks on the skull fit the old account. I’ve left a page open for the Herald.
dialogue.chronicler-ichor-offer.page1 = Some nights the moon sends its Herald. They say it lit the fields with a burning scythe and left no blood behind, only ichor.
dialogue.chronicler-ichor-waiting.bye = See you later.
dialogue.chronicler-ichor-waiting.page1 = Keep the bottle stoppered. I’ve heard three people describe that fire, and by the third telling I could almost see it myself.
dialogue.chronicler-lamp-offer.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.chronicler-lamp-offer.bye = See you later.
dialogue.chronicler-lamp-offer.previous = Tavin. He spent the night in the ditch under my window, and he doesn’t blame me. That’s almost worse.
dialogue.chronicler-lamp-offer.page1 = I’ll sign the page, and the whole village will know it wasn’t the oil. But signing lights nothing.
dialogue.chronicler-lamp-offer.page2 = I want a light on the square, every Blood Moon, that nobody can blow out. Not even me. Bring me a tinkerer’s lamp, and I’ll put all my savings into it.
dialogue.chronicler-lamp-waiting.bye = See you later.
dialogue.chronicler-lamp-waiting.page1 = A tinkerer’s lamp keeps burning when the wind gets in. That’s the light the square needs.
dialogue.chronicler-lamp-ready.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.chronicler-lamp-ready.bye = See you later.
dialogue.chronicler-lamp-ready.previous = Tavin. He spent the night in the ditch under my window, and he doesn’t blame me. That’s almost worse.
dialogue.chronicler-lamp-ready.context = I’ll sign the page, but signing lights nothing. I want a light on the square that nobody can blow out, not even me. Bring me a tinkerer’s lamp, and I’ll put all my savings into it.
dialogue.chronicler-lamp-ready.page1 = Is that a tinkerer’s lamp? It hasn’t flickered once since you came in.
dialogue.chronicler-lamp-handoff.act = Here, take what I brought.
dialogue.chronicler-lamp-handoff.bye = See you later.
dialogue.chronicler-lamp-handoff.page1 = Here is the money, everything I had put aside. We’ll set the lamp on the square, where it can be seen from the road.
dialogue.chronicler-lamp-thanks.bye = See you later.
dialogue.chronicler-lamp-thanks.page1 = The lamp burns on the square. I signed the page, and under my name I wrote Tavin’s: the one who knocked.
dialogue.chronicler-page-offer.act = I’ll talk to him.
dialogue.chronicler-page-offer.bye = See you later.
dialogue.chronicler-page-offer.previous = The Herald’s page is written. Every account in this ledger has its proof now. Every account but one.
dialogue.chronicler-page-offer.page1 = I sent you after a skull to prove a story I already knew was true. One account in the ledger has no name. It’s mine.
dialogue.chronicler-page-offer.page2 = Before that night, I didn’t believe in the Tyrant. On the last Blood Moon, I watched the lanterns die one by one from my window. When only mine was left, I blew it out before dawn. I wanted to see.
dialogue.chronicler-page-offer.page3 = The Tyrant came. The village fought until sunrise. Everyone believes the last lantern ran out of oil.
dialogue.chronicler-page-offer.page4 = I stayed hidden. Someone knocked at my door, and I didn’t open it. Tavin was on the road that night. I never found the courage to ask him what he saw. You can.
dialogue.chronicler-page-waiting.bye = See you later.
dialogue.chronicler-page-waiting.page1 = Tavin came in by the old road that night. If he saw a window go dark, it was mine.
dialogue.chronicler-page-tavin.act = I’ll tell her.
dialogue.chronicler-page-tavin.bye = See you later.
dialogue.chronicler-page-tavin.page1 = The last Blood Moon? I was bringing in the last wagon. I watched the village lanterns die one by one.
dialogue.chronicler-page-tavin.page2 = I know the rule. I ran for the last lit window. It went out as I got there. Dawn was still an hour off.
dialogue.chronicler-page-tavin.page3 = I knocked. Nothing. Then the Tyrant stepped out of the dark. I spent the rest of the night in the ditch under that window.
dialogue.chronicler-page-tavin.page4 = I’ve walked the ditch side ever since, and this hand has never been right. Yselle sent you? So she was inside. I thought the oil had run out and she’d gone to shelter with the others. Tell her I don’t blame her.
dialogue.chronicler-knock-report.act = It was Tavin. He spent the night in the ditch under your window. He doesn’t blame you.
dialogue.chronicler-knock-report.bye = Not yet.
dialogue.chronicler-knock-report.page1 = You’ve seen Tavin? Then tell me. Who knocked?
dialogue.mechanic-gland-ready.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.mechanic-gland-ready.bye = See you later.
dialogue.mechanic-gland-ready.context = My cousin Sprocket says a queen sleeps underneath his drills. When she wakes, the whole shaft rattles. I need a look at one of her glands.
dialogue.mechanic-gland-ready.page1 = What’s that pulsing through your bag? Have you been down where Sprocket found the queen?
dialogue.mechanic-gland-handoff.act = Here, take what I brought.
dialogue.mechanic-gland-handoff.bye = See you later.
dialogue.mechanic-gland-handoff.page1 = Put it in this tray. I’d like to get a good look and keep my fingers.
dialogue.mechanic-gland-offer.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.mechanic-gland-offer.bye = See you later.
dialogue.mechanic-gland-offer.page1 = My cousin Sprocket says a queen sleeps underneath his drills. When she wakes, the whole shaft rattles. I need a look at one of her glands.
dialogue.mechanic-gland-waiting.bye = See you later.
dialogue.mechanic-gland-waiting.page1 = The gland comes from the queen herself. When Sprocket’s drill calls for help, go down with it.
dialogue.mechanic-flare-ready.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.mechanic-flare-ready.bye = See you later.
dialogue.mechanic-flare-ready.previous = There’s grit from the drill in the gland. Sprocket was closer to her nest than he thought.
dialogue.mechanic-flare-ready.context = When a drill goes quiet, Sprocket watches the sky for a flare. I want one by my door. I’ve got eight chunks of deep ore to trade for it.
dialogue.mechanic-flare-ready.page1 = That looks like a flare Sprocket would trust. Do you want to trade it for the ore?
dialogue.mechanic-flare-handoff.act = Here, take what I brought.
dialogue.mechanic-flare-handoff.bye = See you later.
dialogue.mechanic-flare-handoff.page1 = Here’s the ore we agreed on. Set the flare beside it so I can check the fuse.
dialogue.mechanic-flare-offer.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.mechanic-flare-offer.bye = See you later.
dialogue.mechanic-flare-offer.previous = There’s grit from the drill in the gland. Sprocket was closer to her nest than he thought.
dialogue.mechanic-flare-offer.page1 = When a drill goes quiet, Sprocket watches the sky for a flare. I want one by my door. I’ve got eight chunks of deep ore to trade for it.
dialogue.mechanic-flare-waiting.bye = See you later.
dialogue.mechanic-flare-waiting.page1 = Keep the fuse dry on the way here. I’ve got the ore weighed out.
dialogue.mechanic-flare-thanks.bye = See you later.
dialogue.mechanic-flare-thanks.page1 = The flare goes by the door. Next time a drill goes quiet, Sprocket will see it above the treetops before I’ve reached the path.
dialogue.merchant-gold-ready.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.merchant-gold-ready.bye = See you later.
dialogue.merchant-gold-ready.context = A goblin lifted my savings while I was counting sacks of flour. Three bars of gold would let me pay the wagoner this week.
dialogue.merchant-gold-ready.page1 = I know that weight by the way you set your pack down. Could you spare any gold for the wagon bill?
dialogue.merchant-gold-handoff.act = Here, take what I brought.
dialogue.merchant-gold-handoff.bye = See you later.
dialogue.merchant-gold-handoff.page1 = Let’s weigh what you have. My good scales were too heavy for him to steal.
dialogue.merchant-gold-offer.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.merchant-gold-offer.bye = See you later.
dialogue.merchant-gold-offer.page1 = A goblin lifted my savings while I was counting sacks of flour. Three bars of gold would let me pay the wagoner this week.
dialogue.merchant-gold-waiting.bye = See you later.
dialogue.merchant-gold-waiting.page1 = The bill’s still under the flour scoop. I moved the scoop an inch this morning. That’s as far as I got.
dialogue.merchant-sack-ready.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.merchant-sack-ready.bye = See you later.
dialogue.merchant-sack-ready.previous = The wagoner’s bill is paid. I still remember the stitches on my sack.
dialogue.merchant-sack-ready.context = I patched my money sack with blue thread. If you catch up with the goblin, look under the flap.
dialogue.merchant-sack-ready.page1 = Wait, is that blue thread under the flap? Let me see the sack you’ve got.
dialogue.merchant-sack-handoff.act = Here, take what I brought.
dialogue.merchant-sack-handoff.bye = See you later.
dialogue.merchant-sack-handoff.page1 = The stitches are crooked where I finished by candlelight. I remember every one.
dialogue.merchant-sack-offer.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.merchant-sack-offer.bye = See you later.
dialogue.merchant-sack-offer.previous = The wagoner’s bill is paid. I still remember the stitches on my sack.
dialogue.merchant-sack-offer.page1 = I patched my money sack with blue thread. If you catch up with the goblin, look under the flap.
dialogue.merchant-sack-waiting.bye = See you later.
dialogue.merchant-sack-waiting.page1 = When you hear the coins spill, keep your eyes on the goblin. That’s how he got ahead of me.
dialogue.merchant-sack-thanks.bye = See you later.
dialogue.merchant-sack-thanks.page1 = I’ve hung the sack behind the counter. I’m keeping the coins in a box with a lock now.
dialogue.veteran-captain-offer.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.veteran-captain-offer.bye = See you later.
dialogue.veteran-captain-offer.page1 = Look for the brute who calls the charge. Drop that one, and the next wagon has a chance.
dialogue.veteran-captain-waiting.bye = See you later.
dialogue.veteran-captain-waiting.page1 = Don’t let the first rush turn your back to the road. The captain comes in once the others have softened you up.
dialogue.veteran-captain-thanks.bye = See you later.
dialogue.veteran-captain-thanks.page1 = A wagon made it through before noon. I heard the wheels in the dry ruts. Never thought I’d miss that racket.
dialogue.veteran-lamp-thanks.bye = See you later.
dialogue.veteran-lamp-thanks.page1 = There’s a lamp on the square that never goes out. I walk the middle of the road again.
dialogue.armorer-warlord-ready.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.armorer-warlord-ready.bye = See you later.
dialogue.armorer-warlord-ready.context = I want to see how a complete Warlord suit sits on the stand. The last piece I saw had deep ore worked right into the plate.
dialogue.armorer-warlord-ready.page1 = That tint looks like blood shard. Have you brought any of the Warlord plates?
dialogue.armorer-warlord-handoff.act = Here, take what I brought.
dialogue.armorer-warlord-handoff.bye = See you later.
dialogue.armorer-warlord-handoff.page1 = Put them on the stand. Once the suit is whole, we’ll see where the weight goes.
dialogue.armorer-warlord-offer.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.armorer-warlord-offer.bye = See you later.
dialogue.armorer-warlord-offer.page1 = I want to see how a complete Warlord suit sits on the stand. The last piece I saw had deep ore worked right into the plate.
dialogue.armorer-warlord-waiting.bye = See you later.
dialogue.armorer-warlord-waiting.page1 = Set the plates out before you rivet them. It’s easier to see a bad bend in good light.
dialogue.armorer-moonfang-ready.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.armorer-moonfang-ready.bye = See you later.
dialogue.armorer-moonfang-ready.previous = The fit is better than I expected. Now I’d like to see how a Moonfang Staff balances in the hand.
dialogue.armorer-moonfang-ready.context = That armor taught me how the plates take a blow. Bring me a Moonfang Staff so I can see how its grip sits in a caster’s hand.
dialogue.armorer-moonfang-ready.page1 = That staff catches the light like the Warlord plates. Is it the Moonfang?
dialogue.armorer-moonfang-handoff.act = Here, take what I brought.
dialogue.armorer-moonfang-handoff.bye = See you later.
dialogue.armorer-moonfang-handoff.page1 = Lay it on the leather. I can feel warmth coming off the grip.
dialogue.armorer-moonfang-offer.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.armorer-moonfang-offer.bye = See you later.
dialogue.armorer-moonfang-offer.previous = The fit is better than I expected. Now I’d like to see how a Moonfang Staff balances in the hand.
dialogue.armorer-moonfang-offer.page1 = That armor taught me how the plates take a blow. Bring me a Moonfang Staff so I can see how its grip sits in a caster’s hand.
dialogue.armorer-moonfang-waiting.bye = See you later.
dialogue.armorer-moonfang-waiting.page1 = The Arcane Bench will do the careful work. Pay attention to where the staff balances.
dialogue.armorer-moonfang-thanks.bye = See you later.
dialogue.armorer-moonfang-thanks.page1 = The weight sits forward of the grip. My first walking staff wore smooth just below the wrap. Now I know where to start the next one.
dialogue.scout-sapling-ready.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.scout-sapling-ready.bye = See you later.
dialogue.scout-sapling-ready.context = The turn in the path needs shade. Living sap will help the roots settle, and a potted sapling can put down the first ones.
dialogue.scout-sapling-ready.page1 = I smell sap. Are those supplies for the little tree at the turn?
dialogue.scout-sapling-handoff.act = Here, take what I brought.
dialogue.scout-sapling-handoff.bye = See you later.
dialogue.scout-sapling-handoff.page1 = Set what you brought in the shade here. I’ll keep everything damp until we’re ready to plant.
dialogue.scout-sapling-offer.act = I’ll do it.
dialogue.scout-sapling-offer.bye = See you later.
dialogue.scout-sapling-offer.page1 = The turn in the path needs shade. Living sap will help the roots settle, and a potted sapling can put down the first ones.
dialogue.scout-sapling-waiting.bye = See you later.
dialogue.scout-sapling-waiting.page1 = The home tree shelters the little ones. You may have to wait for the village to call them home.
dialogue.scout-sapling-thanks.bye = See you later.
dialogue.scout-sapling-thanks.page1 = I moved the stone to give the roots room. There’s a place to sit beside it now. A little one can try it first.
